# Security standards

This product is a **multi-tenant SaaS** platform handling private source code, documentation,
and credentials. Security is not optional.

## Secrets & tokens
- **Never commit secrets.** Document variables in `.env.example`; real `.env` is git/cursor-ignored.
- Repo and integration tokens are **encrypted at rest**; decrypt only in memory when needed
  (e.g. a sync worker).
- Prefer **least-privilege, read-only** tokens for connected repositories where applicable.
- **Never log** secrets, tokens, passwords, or full sensitive request bodies.

## Access control
- Enforce **RBAC** and **tenant isolation** at the API and data boundaries; scope queries by
  organization/project as required.
- **Audit-log** sensitive and administrative actions (actor, action, target, timestamp).
- **Parameterized queries only**; sanitize/validate all inputs (see `database-standards.mdc`).

## Deployment posture
- Do not invent hosting or vendor constraints. If a security-sensitive capability needs a
  commercial or third-party service, **ask** or write an ADR before adding it.
